The QFXLM Engine repository contains multiple scheduled processors.

Each scheduler follows an existing framework involving:

- A processor extending "AbstractProcessor"
- Scheduler business-object configuration
- Spring Batch job configuration
- A tasklet invoking "runProcess()"
- Scheduler event registration and triggering
- Existing database and MQ utilities

The framework invokes the registered processor when the configured scheduler time is reached.

Mohan explicitly instructed that the new Netting scheduler must follow the existing GI Release Scheduler pattern.

Do not introduce another scheduling framework.

Do not introduce "@Scheduled", new Quartz infrastructure, independent threads, executors, Spring Boot scheduling configuration or unnecessary components.

Business purpose

This is a recovery/release scheduler.

A GI message may already have been generated in the database but not successfully published to the external GI partner because of an earlier failure or interruption.

The Netting scheduler should:

1. Run through the existing Engine scheduling framework.
2. Retrieve eligible Netting GI messages from Oracle.
3. Publish those messages to the configured GI partner queue through the existing MQ mechanism.
4. Update their release status in the database using the new Netting procedure.
5. Report accurate success/failure results.

The existing MM implementation is the reference for behavior.

