- Use the existing message DTO structure.
- Use the existing intermediate status value "Constants.GI_INT_STATUS".
- Check the Netting procedure's success flag.
- Capture and report the error message on failure.
- Close JDBC resources properly.
- Ensure a failed DB update is reported as a failure.

The new helper should be placed in the smallest appropriate existing or Netting-specific location.

Do not create an entire new DAO framework merely for this procedure.

Updated-count requirement

The Netting procedure's fourth parameter does not return the updated count.

Do not fabricate one.

Do not treat the size of the submitted message list as proof that every database row was updated.

If the existing success/failure reporting depends on an actual updated count, adapt the Netting processor to report what is verifiable, or ask for clarification if the acceptance criteria require an exact database-updated count.

